## Model card

- **Name:** Big Pickle
- **Short description:** OpenCode Zen’s long-running free stealth slot (`opencode/big-pickle`, 200K context, text-only, $0) with disputed and historically unstable underlying model identity/checkpoint behavior.
- **Provider / access:** OpenCode Zen free stealth tier. OpenCode docs/changelog describe Zen/provider access but do not publish a stable official model card/spec page for `big-pickle` as a named model.
- **Release / knowledge:** Not officially announced as a stable, versioned named model; evidence indicates the underlying checkpoint may change in place over time. Knowledge cutoff not stated.
- **IDs:** `big-pickle`, `opencode/big-pickle`.
- **Context window:** 200,000 tokens total (32,000 max output) per local metadata; not independently confirmed by an official stable model card in this pass.
- **Modalities:** Text input/output (per metadata/community usage context).
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-11):** Free $0/$0/$0 on OpenCode Zen (no published end date in reviewed sources/metadata); local metadata notes data may be used to improve the model during free period.
- **Architecture:** Undisclosed/disputed and potentially mutable; no stable public architecture disclosure.

### Raw benchmarks found

> SECOND-PASS SELF-EXCLUSION (updated): I performed a deep second-pass review using alternative web access (`webfetch`, PowerShell HTTP/API fetches) across official OpenCode sources, GitHub issues/releases, models.dev/OpenRouter lookups, and community/search endpoints. `big-pickle` is consistently evidenced as a stealth/experimental free slot in OpenCode Zen, but I found no official model card, no stable provider spec sheet, and no independently verifiable, clearly attributable standardized benchmark numerics for this exact slot/checkpoint aligned with this repository’s required categories (SWE-bench, Terminal-Bench, GPQA, AIME, LiveCodeBench, etc.). Community reports also indicate identity/behavior changes and quality issues, making attribution unreliable. This file remains `.md.excluded` (notes only; scores ignored).

